*...+....1....+....2....+....3....+....4....+....5....+....6....+....7....+....8
TITLE
1 MeV photon point source, pencil beam, on 2 cm lead slab in vacuum
DEFAULTS                                                              PRECISIO
*
BEAM          -0.001                                                  PHOTON
BEAMPOS          0.0       0.0     -10.0
*
GEOBEGIN                                                              COMBNAME
    0    0
RPP world      -100.0 +100.0 -100.0 +100.0 -100.0 +100.0
RPP fillbox     -50.0  +50.0  -50.0  +50.0  -50.0  +50.0
RPP leadslb     -20.0  +20.0  -20.0  +20.0    0.0    2.0
END
regBH        5 +world -fillbox
regFILL      5 +fillbox -leadslb
regLEAD      5 +leadslb
END
GEOEND
*
ASSIGNMA    BLCKHOLE     regBH
ASSIGNMA      VACUUM   regFILL
ASSIGNMA        LEAD   regLEAD
*
* Electron/positron and photon transport and production thresholds
EMFCUT        -1E-06      1E-6             regFILL  @LASTREG
EMFCUT        -1E-06      1E-6            BLCKHOLE  @LASTMAT          PROD-CUT
*
* Dose in a box enclosing the lead slab
USRBIN          10.0      DOSE       -30      20.0      20.0      10.0DOSEBOX
USRBIN         -20.0     -20.0      -5.0        40        40        30&
*
* Track-length photon fluence in the lead slab
USRTRACK        -1.0    PHOTON       -31   regLEAD    3200.0          TRKFLU
USRTRACK      1.0E-3    1.0E-6        -6                              &
*
* Boundary-crossing photon fluence from vacuum into the lead slab
* WHAT(6) = slab surface 2*(40*40) + 4*(40*2) = 3520 cm2
USRBDX           99.    PHOTON       -32   regFILL   regLEAD    3520.0FILEAD
USRBDX        1.0E-3    1.0E-6       120       0.0                    &
*
* Energy deposition in the same box as the dose scorer
USRBIN          10.0    ENERGY       -33      20.0      20.0      10.0EDEPBOX
USRBIN         -20.0     -20.0      -5.0        40        40        30&
*
RANDOMIZ         1.0    918273
START         1000.0
STOP
